.TH TUI_KEYTABLE_INIT 3 2026-10-18 "libtuikit 0.10" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_keytable_init, tui_keytable_find, tui_registry_verb, tui_key_reserved,
tui_keycode_of, tui_keycode_name, tui_nav_key, tui_actionmenu_open,
tui_actionmenu_run, tui_actionmenu_handle, tui_actionmenu_render,
tui_actionmenu_free, tui_keyhelp_open, tui_keyhelp_free \- the key table,
the action menu and the help made from the table
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/actions.h>
.PP
.BI "int  tui_keytable_init(tui_keytable *" t ", const tui_keyentry *" entries ", int " n ,
.BI "                       char *" why ", size_t " size );
.BI "int  tui_keytable_find(const tui_keytable *" t ", const char *" view ,
.BI "                       const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "tui_verb    tui_registry_verb(tui_keycode " key );
.BI "int         tui_key_reserved(tui_keycode " key );
.BI "tui_keycode tui_keycode_of(const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "int         tui_keycode_name(tui_keycode " key ", char *" buf ", size_t " size );
.BI "tui_nav     tui_nav_key(const tui_event *" ev ", int " depth );
.PP
.BI "int  tui_actionmenu_open(tui_actionmenu *" m ", const tui_keytable *" t ,
.BI "                         const char *" view ", const char *" target );
.BI "int  tui_actionmenu_run(tui_actionmenu *" m ", const tui_keytable *" t ,
.BI "                        int " entry ", const char *" target );
.BI "tui_action_state tui_actionmenu_handle(tui_actionmenu *" m ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_actionmenu_render(tui_actionmenu *" m ", tui_canvas " c );
.BI "void tui_actionmenu_free(tui_actionmenu *" m );
.PP
.BI "int  tui_keyhelp_open(tui_keyhelp *" h ", const tui_keytable *" t ,
.BI "                      const char *" view ", const char *" title );
.BI "void tui_keyhelp_free(tui_keyhelp *" h );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions carry the keyboard policy of the terminal interfaces
(policies/tui-interface-model.md, "Actions that change state: the action
menu").
A program writes everything its keys do as one array of
.IR tui_keyentry :
the view, the direct key (or
.BR TUI_KC_NONE ,
the menu only), the registry verb, the action's name and description, its
class
.RB ( TUI_ACT_HARMLESS ", " TUI_ACT_ROUTINE ", " TUI_ACT_SERIOUS ", " TUI_ACT_RARE ),
whether it is irreversible, the question to confirm with, and the program's
own id.
Keys are
.I tui_keycode
numbers: a character is its code point, a special key is its
.I tui_key
value, Ctrl+letter is
.B TUI_KC_CTRL
or-ed with the letter.
The names
.BR TUI_KC_STAR " (*), " TUI_KC_JUNK " (!), " TUI_KC_READ " (+), " TUI_KC_UNREAD " (\-),"
.BR TUI_KC_DELETE_D " (d), " TUI_KC_DELETE " (Delete)"
are the registry;
.BR TUI_KC_NEW ", " TUI_KC_EDIT ", " TUI_KC_MOVE ", " TUI_KC_MESSAGE
are n, e, t, m; the others name the common table
.RB ( TUI_KC_BACK ", " TUI_KC_HELP ", " TUI_KC_MENU ", " TUI_KC_RELOAD ", " TUI_KC_QUIT
and so on).
.TP
.BR tui_keytable_init ()
Validates the table; the program calls it at start and exits on \-1
(errno EINVAL, the reason in
.I why
when it is not NULL).
It refuses: a state-changing entry whose direct key is not in the registry,
or is the registry key of another verb; a harmless entry on a registry key
(a key that changes state is never also harmless); a serious or irreversible
entry without a confirmation containing
.BR %s ,
where the target is put; a rare entry with a direct key; one key bound twice
in one view; an entry without a name; a view description of more than three
lines or a second one for a view (below).
The array is not copied.
.IP
A row with no
.IR action ,
no key and only
.I desc
set (and
.I view
the view it describes, NULL for every view) is the
.B description of a view
(one to three lines, wrapped to 64 columns, in the program's language of the
screen).
.TP
.BR tui_keytable_find ()
The index of the entry bound to the event in
.IR view ,
or \-1.
The key handler is driven by this, and the help is made from the same array.
.TP
.BR tui_registry_verb "(), " tui_key_reserved ()
The verb a registry key stands for; whether a key is in the reserved
harmless set (r s f p o c a u i l h x / j k q g G U ? :), which no program
gives a state-changing meaning.
.TP
.BR tui_keycode_of "(), " tui_keycode_name ()
The code of a key event (none for Alt and for modified special keys); the
name of a code ("d", "Delete", "ctrl\-c", "Space") with the length returned
as by snprintf(3).
.TP
.BR tui_nav_key ()
The way out: q and Backspace go back and never quit (nothing at depth 0); Esc goes
back, and at depth 0, the top level with nothing open, quits; ctrl-c quits
from anywhere.
Call it only from views where no text field has the cursor: Backspace in a
field stays a delete.
Returns
.BR TUI_NAV_BACK ", " TUI_NAV_QUIT " or " TUI_NAV_NONE .
.TP
.BR tui_actionmenu_open ()
The menu that ':' opens: every non-harmless action of the view, each with
its name, description and its direct key beside it.
The program gives it events first while it is open
.RB ( tui_actionmenu_handle ())
and draws it last
.RB ( tui_actionmenu_render ()).
.I m\->state
becomes
.B TUI_ACTION_CHOSEN
(run entry
.IR m\->entry )
or
.BR TUI_ACTION_CANCELLED .
An action that needs a confirmation opens a dialog named after the action,
its text the entry's question with the target put in, the default answer No.
Enter on the default, Esc and ctrl-c cancel; only Yes (or y) chooses.
.TP
.BR tui_actionmenu_run ()
The same for an entry reached by its direct key: chosen at once when it
needs no confirmation, otherwise the confirmation is open.
.TP
.BR tui_keyhelp_open ()
The help overlay of a view, a
.I tui_dialog
in
.IR h\->dialog ,
with a row for every entry that has a direct key there.
The description row of the view, if the table has one, is shown wrapped
between the title and the keys, followed by a blank row; a view without one
shows the keys only.
.PP
All return 0 on success and \-1 with errno set on failure (EINVAL, ENOMEM).
The library prints nothing.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
static const tui_keyentry keys[] = {
    { "list", TUI_KC_STAR, TUI_VERB_STAR, "Star", NULL,
      TUI_ACT_ROUTINE, 0, NULL, 1 },
    { "list", TUI_KC_DELETE_D, TUI_VERB_DELETE, "Delete", NULL,
      TUI_ACT_SERIOUS, 1, "Delete %s? This cannot be undone.", 2 },
    { "list", TUI_KC_NONE, TUI_VERB_NONE, "Rotate secret", NULL,
      TUI_ACT_RARE, 0, NULL, 3 },
};
    { "list", TUI_KC_NONE, TUI_VERB_NONE, NULL,
      "The messages of the folder; the cursor is on one.  Enter opens it.",
      TUI_ACT_HARMLESS, 0, NULL, 0 },
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_dialog_message (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
